==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|longshot}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-au-long shot.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|nautical}} Something [[unlikely]]; something that has little [[chance]] of happening or working. The term arose from the accuracy of early ship guns, which were effective only at close range and unlikely to hit the mark at any great distance.
#: ''We can try your plan, but it's a '''long shot''' and it probably won't work.''
# {{lb|en|film}} A [[master]] shot, the primary wide [[shot]] of a [[scene]] into which the [[closeup]]s will be edited later.

